+# Code-stage change log (gomoku-r1)
+
+This file tracks changes made at the code stage for the gomoku
+requirement.  Each section corresponds to one running cycle (one
+requeue cycle = one r{N} directory).
+
+## Cycle: gomoku-r1 (requeue-after-FAIL)
+
+**Status at cycle start**: code-review FAIL on `gomoku-r1-review.md`
+(plan §9 explains the requeue; this cycle's plan re-incorporated the
+previous PASS review's suggestions).
+
+**This directory supersedes** the previous r1 code (kept under
+`workspace/gomoku/code/gomoku-r1/` until overwritten; the old review
+file `gomoku-r1-review.md` is the input for this cycle).
+
+### Fixes applied in this cycle
+
+1. **FR-07 forbidden-move — extended live-three detection** (critical,
+   fixes review opinion 1 / UTB-10/15):
+   - Previous `Board._is_live_three` used a fixed 5-cell window that
+     missed the `..XXX_` "extension" shape (placed stone fills the
+     third cell of an existing 2-stone run with two open ends).
+   - New implementation uses `run + open_ends` for the run passing
+     through the placed stone, plus explicit broken-pattern detection
+     (`X_XX`, `XX_X`).  See `board.py:_is_live_three` and
+     `_has_broken_live_three` and the comment block above
+     `_count_live_threes`.
+
+2. **`Board.undo` returns bool** (plan §4 / UTB-28 / UTB-29):
+   - Previous signature returned `None` and silently no-op'd.
+   - New signature: `True` if a stone was removed; `False` on
+     out-of-bounds / empty cell / non-int input.  Matches `place`'s
+     style and the testplan.
+
+3. **`parse_move` regex widened** (UTB-07 vs UTB-08 reconciliation):
+   - Old regex `^[A-Oa-o][1-9][0-5]?$` rejected `A16` as format; new
+     regex `^[A-Oa-o][1-9]\d?$` accepts `A1..A99` (with leading
+     1-9), so `A16` correctly reports `out_of_range` and `A0` reports
+     `format` — both match UTB-07/08 verbatim.
+
+4. **AI explicit downgrade chain** (plan §5.3 / testplan UTA-11):
+   - Previous `choose_move` had iterative deepening but no explicit
+     depth/candidate reduction on timeout.
+   - New `_strong_move` has three levels: full (20/4, 1.5 s) → reduce
+     (15/3, 0.9 s) → fallback to one-ply candidate winner.
+   - `_alpha_beta_search` extracted as a single-pass search helper for
+     reuse across levels.
+
+### Other changes
+
+5. `ui.py` last-move marker strengthened from `underline` to
+   `bold reverse` so the marker is visible on `NO_COLOR` / dumb
+   terminals (FR-08 robustness).
+6. `__init__.py` version bumped to `0.2.0`.
+7. `__main__.py` no longer calls `main()` with no arguments; passes
+   `sys.argv[1:]` explicitly (was raising SystemExit with no args;
+   now argparse exit code 2 on bad args).
+
+### Validation performed (this cycle)
+
+* `python3 -m py_compile gomoku/*.py` — all green.
+* `python3 -m gomoku --help` — argparse works, defaults match README.
+* Manual sanity script (see git history) — all forbidden-move cases
+  (overline, double-four, double-three, five-overrides, white
+  immunity, parse_move errors, undo bool, win detection 4 directions,
+  is_full) pass.
+* AI smoke tests: weak / medium / strong tiers all return legal moves;
+  medium blocks live-three and rush-four threats correctly; strong
+  with 0.05 s budget completes in ≤ 100 ms via the downgrade chain.
+
+### Out of scope / not changed
+
+* The rules engine was already correct in the previous cycle (review
+  PASS on items 1, 2, 4-10).  No change to `check_win`, `place`,
+  `is_full`, `parse_move` (apart from regex tweak above), `_DIRECTIONS`.
+* The UI and main loop were not changed structurally; only the
+  last-move marker style was strengthened.
